{"metadata":{"externalID":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","role":"collection","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") for a Google Analytics 4 stream in one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call. It checks the measurement ID and the API secret, and posts to the Measurement Protocol’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/mp\/collect"},{"text":" endpoint of the region (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". It splits each batch to the Measurement Protocol’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"): 25 events and 100 KB a request. A batch with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-API-secret-stays-on-a-server","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"The API secret stays on a server"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol takes only requests that carry one of the stream’s API secrets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding that secret can send events to the property. Google’s docs say not to expose it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app, and an app’s binary can be read by anyone who installs it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So the whole module is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, where a server runs. An app for iOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iPadOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS or Mac Catalyst that calls the factory, or names the encoder, fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to compile. A Mac app, AppKit or SwiftUI, compiles the factory as a Mac server does, but the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory refuses it at run time: it throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"process’s main bundle is an ","type":"text"},{"code":".app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".appex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Nothing stops a Mac app from building an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with this encoder and an endpoint it writes itself, secret and all, so don’t.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The secret is also in the query of every request’s URL. Don’t log the destination, its requests or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a transport’s URLs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","type":"reference"},{"text":" for an empty measurement ID, for one that isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"G-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" followed by uppercase letters and digits, and for an empty API secret. The region has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default: ","type":"text"},{"code":".global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is Google’s default endpoint, and ","type":"text"},{"code":".eu","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has Google collect the data in the EU.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Getting-an-apps-events-to-Google-Analytics","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Getting an app’s events to Google Analytics"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app’s events reach Google Analytics through a server of yours: the app sends them there, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the server makes this destination and hands it the records. Traffluent doesn’t provide that server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yet. TraffluentCollector receives an app’s batches, but it doesn’t forward them to Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analytics, and Traffluent has no decoder that turns a collector batch back into records."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Until it does, the server’s job is:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read each event the app sent (its name, version, identifier, timestamp, properties and session)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decode it into the same "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type the app tracked, from a module the app and the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Remake its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord(id:event:timestamp:sourceLocation:context:)"},{"text":": the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app’s identifier and timestamp, and a context whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":" is the app’s session.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand each batch of records to the destination’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t track the events again through a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":" on the server. That tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would give every event the server’s own session, so every user of the app would arrive in Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analytics as one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A server that tracks its own events, rather than an app’s, uses a tracker as any app does:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)","\/\/ A server tracking its own events: its sessions are the server's.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: googleAnalytics)"]},{"anchor":"What-Google-Analytics-receives","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Google Analytics receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request holds one client’s events, as the Measurement Protocol takes one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, written as the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"halves of its UUID in decimal, joined by a period, the form the Measurement Protocol asks for. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, in a request of its own. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"text":" parameter is the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, so Google Analytics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"groups the session’s events, and its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"text":" is the record’s timestamp. Every request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends ad consent as denied, so Google uses none of the events for advertising.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"text":", user properties, location, IP address, device or user agent is sent, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"advertising identifier. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and standard context aren’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent either. Google Analytics counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports, and so is each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engagement_time_msec"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t measure engagement. Without it the events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"don’t count toward engagement time or engaged sessions, and the Realtime and Users reports can show"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no users while events arrive. Check the event counts, not the user counts, to see that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination works."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and become the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"params","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans, so a nested value is spread into a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"cart_size","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tags_0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-sent-twice","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records sent twice"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics can’t tell a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"repeat from a new event, and counts every one it receives. A record is sent more than once when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request is retried after Google stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each such record is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted twice in Google Analytics."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name, or a parameter’s name, is longer than 40 bytes, doesn’t start with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"letter, or holds anything but letters, numbers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Google Analytics keeps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_start"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first_visit"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its reserved names), or takes only from an app stream ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_view"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_impression"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in_app_purchase"},{"type":"text","text":");"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a parameter Google Analytics keeps (a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"firebase_"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ga_"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"google_"},{"text":" prefix) or named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"text":", which the encoder writes;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one of more than 25 parameters, counting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", or with a string longer than 100 bytes;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one tracked more than 71 hours before the batch is encoded, or more than 15 minutes after it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and one whose timestamp has no microseconds form;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one too large for a request."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Google Analytics wouldn’t refuse such an event: it answers 2xx either way. Under its default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relaxed validation it stores the event without the parameter that breaks a rule, or under a name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it never checked, so the report would hold an event other than the one tracked. The encoder leaves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the record out and reports it instead. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of up to 500","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The encoder logs a notice for each event and property of the plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named as Google Analytics refuses when the destination is made; rename such an event or property,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raising the event’s version, to send it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-the-Measurement-Protocol-doesnt-report","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the Measurement Protocol doesn’t report"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, including one it can’t read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose events it doesn’t store. A wrong measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored, so check the property’s Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. Google’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validation server, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/debug\/mp\/collect"},{"text":", checks a body’s shape but not the measurement ID or the API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"secret, so a body it accepts can still be stored nowhere. A record older than 72 hours is stored as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"if it happened 72 hours ago, so the encoder leaves out one older than 71 hours, the hour to spare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the request to reach Google and clocks that disagree. A request is encoded once and retried as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it is, so the encoder gives each request a deadline 71 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request still failing by then isn’t sent again: the destination drops the whole request, its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"younger records too, and reports it on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or Segment, use "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"SegmentSpecEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Google Analytics receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Google Analytics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Google-Analytics"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"references":{"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError":{"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsencodingerror","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"symbol","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsRegion":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where Google Analytics collects a stream’s events, which decides the Measurement Protocol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"endpoint they are posted to."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsregion","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"}],"title":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticssetuperror","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"}],"title":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}],"type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/googleanalytics(measurementid:apisecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"measurementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", authenticated by its "},{"code":"apiSecret","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},